comments.body:
**Fixed in #752** (merge 8277233f85).

Under Aggressive, the prompt now leaves Grant once out, and the prompt and denial say why, when the command's text shows every file it writes and none of them is something Grant once lifts. That covers:
- writes outside the current folder: `echo t04 >> ../outside-notes.txt`, `/tmp`;
- writes to a read-only part of the folder: the project's `.git`, as in `printf … > .git/hooks/pre-commit` and `git config core.hooksPath /tmp`;
- `mkdir .agents` (#584 now counts `mkdir`/`rmdir` as writes);
- commands that write nothing liftable: `cat .codex/notes.md`, `ln -s notes.txt notes-link.txt && cat notes-link.txt`.

"Liftable" is decided the same way `ReadDenials::apply` decides it. A command whose writes the text can't show keeps the offer, for example scripts, `npm install`, `cd`, substitutions, `cp -t`, or a variable set for a config writer. The exception is a command that also writes a start-up file outside the folder or `.codex`/`.agents` (#620/#584). Nothing about what runs or what is denied changed, and Permissive and Moderate are unchanged.

**Test:** `issue_736_740.rs::issue_740_no_grant_where_it_cannot_apply` (real sandbox, macOS and glitch). It fails before the fix and passes after.

**Evidence:** tmux replay `qa/security-levels/fixes/issue-736-740-20261014/`, [video](https://github.com/CorbanuCore/CorbanuTerminal/releases/download/demos/issue-740-issue740-no-grant-where-useless-a79ff79b392a-2026-10-13.mp4).
